From d0ea9ffc6342a3b7a4f1aea299c279c41feb1f7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Boyd <swboyd@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 27 Mar 2024 13:27:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/37] clk: qcom: dispcc-sc7180: stop firmware rotator clock
 for TCL ACPI

The SC7180 firmware can leave disp_cc_mdss_rot_clk running from
disp_cc_pll0. Power-cycling the MDSS clock tree while that branch
remains enabled can leave the rotator clock stuck.

Disable the rotator branch before DISPCC PLL setup on the non-OF path.
This adapts Stephen Boyd's force-off-at-probe change carried by qc7. The
TCL adaptation restricts the operation to the ACPI path and propagates a
regmap update failure; the original change applied the operation
unconditionally and did not check that return value.

Original-author: Stephen Boyd <swboyd@chromium.org>
Original-commit: d7fe3796aae4b020c05e02024a03e69bc4c288e0
Link: https://github.com/TravMurav/linux/commit/d7fe3796aae4b020c05e02024a03e69bc4c288e0
TCL adaptation: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>

The original commit is preserved in the qc7 provenance archive.
Attribution here does not assert review or approval of the TCL
adaptation by the original author.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sc7180.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sc7180.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sc7180.c
index 2dd1227f583af0591f1cd4d198c8d3107dc00abd..850cfcf0b58b0dd0a4a2e29ebba5063c22c223c1 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sc7180.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sc7180.c
@@ -771,6 +771,15 @@ static int disp_cc_sc7180_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(regmap))
 		return PTR_ERR(regmap);
 
+	/* Firmware may leave ROT running; stop it before MDSS power cycling. */
+	if (!pdev->dev.of_node) {
+		ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap,
+					disp_cc_mdss_rot_clk.clkr.enable_reg,
+					disp_cc_mdss_rot_clk.clkr.enable_mask, 0);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	/* 1380MHz configuration */
 	disp_cc_pll_config.l = 0x47;
 	disp_cc_pll_config.alpha = 0xe000;
